  aaa authentication enable default local     <cr>
  aaa accounting login default                none / start-stop / stop-only
  aaa accounting commands                     <1-15> privilege level range

  Four facts from this listing:
  1. "tacacs-server host <ip>" takes NO port argument.  It offers only key, vrf and
     <cr>.  TACACS+ on this platform is fixed to TCP port 49.
  2. The shared key can be typed as plain STRING, or given already encrypted with 8
     (DES) or 9 (AES).
  3. "none" is offered for ENABLE authentication and never for LOGIN authentication.
     This matches TFS S1599.1.071, which lists tacacs+, local and none for the enable
     method and no none for login.
  4. "none" is not reachable directly after "default".  It exists only as the fallback
     after "group tacacs+".

