STEP 4 (designed) -- build and prove a way back before the method list is changed     PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: platforms/x960.md section 7E.1 says "local" at the end of a method list is a
  fallback for an UNREACHABLE server, not for a Reject.  The TACACS+ server does not
  know the user "manager".  So the moment the default login list points at TACACS+,
  "manager" can no longer log in to this DUT by any path.  This step creates a local
  account that can still get in, and proves it works first.

awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# username tacuser privilege 15 password <local password>
awplus(config)# end
awplus#

  The local password of "tacuser" is DIFFERENT from its TACACS+ password.  That makes
