  AlliedWare Plus (TM) 0.0.0 10/12/26 06:38:00
  awplus>
  LOGIN RESULT: USER  proto=ssh  user=tacuser  seconds=0.4

  === CMD: show users ===
  Line    User            Host(s)  Idle      Location        Priv Idletime Timeout
  con 0   tacuser         idle     00:00:07  ttyS0           15   10       N/A
  vty 0   tacuser         idle     00:00:00  10.38.22.33     1    10       N/A

  Wire: 29 packets, the same TWO flows per login: 17 packets with 68 B out and 46 B in,
  then 12 packets with 73 B out and 30 B in.

  => STEP 8 PASS: TACACS+ authentication serves the SSH path as well as the console,
     with the same two-flow signature.  Two extra facts.  First, the "Priv" column of
     "show users" is the session's CURRENT privilege, not the user's maximum.  The
     console session reads 15 because it had been enabled.  This fresh SSH session
     reads 1, although the server returned priv-lvl = 15.  So a TACACS+ priv-lvl of 15
     does NOT raise the session automatically; "enable" is still needed.  Second, the
     SSH login's request is 2 bytes larger than the console's for the same credential,
     68 B against 66 B.  STEP 13 explains that.

