  manager@10.38.22.34's password:
  LOGIN RESULT: FAIL  proto=ssh  user=manager  seconds=2.0        (--expect fail: MATCH)

  Wire, tac-mgr-reject.pcap: 17 packets, ONE flow, out 64 B / in 46 B.  Authentication
  only, with no authorization.  That is STEP 7's reject signature, on the SSH path.

  => STEP 10 PASS: "manager" is a local account with privilege 15.  It offered its
     correct local password.  "local" is written at the end of the method list.  It was
     still refused, because the server answers Reject for it.  This is the most
     dangerous property of the feature in daily use, and it is why STEP 4 built a way
     back before the method list was touched.

